{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/849673-2ed-feral-infection","id":849673,"title":"[2ed] Feral Infection","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Chronicles of Darkness","Vampire: The Requiem"],"posts":[{"date":"2016-03-19T03:50:51-07:00","id":849673,"title":"[2ed] Feral Infection","content":"Hi all,<br /> I have a doubt about Feral Infection. This power, when used, works also on the other members of the coterie and allies or the vampire can choose to save someone from its effects? Because I think this power becomes pretty useless in a coterie or am I missing something?<br /> I explain the actual sitation:<br /> In order to save someone tied to a pyre in the middle of a crowd (the setting is requiem for Rome using second edition rules), my players chose to use feral infection to give rise to a riot among the present and, in the confusion of the moment, save them.<br /> I know that there would be better ways to achieve this, like using Majesty on the leader of the soldiers to make them free, but, the general point is, when or how, in a coterie or a group, this power can become useful? And is there a way, for the allies, to avoid the effects?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":7079,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7079-marcus","user":"Marcus","date":". 03-19-2016, 06:55 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7079-marcus","name":"Marcus","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7079_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1119"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-03-19T06:44:19-07:00","id":849693,"title":"","content":"For the allies to avoid the effect, they'd have to either not be in the area, or succeed on the roll. Otherwise, they frenzy and directed by the vampire using Feral Infection.<br /> <br /> How can this be useful in a group? You can warn your party to get away from the area before using it, or, maybe they might be ok with frenzying, especially when their trusted ally/friend can control who they target.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2698-the-storyteller","name":"The Storyteller","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"132"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-03-19T07:13:24-07:00","id":849703,"title":"","content":"I suppose &quot;ride the wave&quot; is not an option here, right?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7079-marcus","name":"Marcus","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7079_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1119"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-03-19T07:17:46-07:00","id":849705,"title":"","content":"EDIT: Nevermind, re-read the power, my suggestion wouldn't work.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Going by Willow now, or Wil for short. She/Her/Hers.","edited":{"userid":269,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/269-charlaquin","user":"Charlaquin","date":". 03-19-2016, 10:21 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/269-charlaquin","name":"Charlaquin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar269_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10831"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-03-19T07:51:11-07:00","id":849712,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Marcus</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/849673-2ed-feral-infection?p=849703#post849703\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I suppose &quot;ride the wave&quot; is not an option here, right?</div> </div> </div> </div>Not unless they have the coil of the dragon that lets you ride the wave reflexively in response to an otherwise involuntary frenzy trigger. I guess they could have ridden the wave <i>before </i>the power was used. But if you're willing to frenzy anyway, why don't you trust your party member to direct you?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2698-the-storyteller","name":"The Storyteller","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"132"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-03-19T08:42:10-07:00","id":849738,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Marcus</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/849673-2ed-feral-infection#post849673\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I know that there would be better ways to achieve this, like using Majesty on the leader of the soldiers to make them free, but, the general point is, when or how, in a coterie or a group, this power can become useful? And is there a way, for the allies, to avoid the effects?</div> </div> </div> </div> How or why is this useful? Swarm attacks. Majesty and Dominate both break if the target takes damage, or if the target makes Integrity/Humanity checks. Neither of them are exceptionally useful as a combat ability, since many people can likely have breaking points related to combat. Oh, the three mental powers will END combats if they take root, but for actual physical brawling? Animalism is your &quot;everyone is my attack swarm!&quot; power.<br /> <br /> To look at your proposed scenario. Majesty could walk up, charm the crowd, get the crowd to release the captive, and everyone go home happy. Animalism is the power you use to infect the crowd, drive them into a riot and turn them against the speaker, and violently tear the leader apart. Both Majesty and Animalism are working the crowds here, but Animalism is the only way you can get a good fight out of the issue.<br /> <br /> Each Discipline has its own &quot;niche.&quot; If you want to direct the crowd as rational beings, that's what Majesty is for. No other magic power in Vampire 2e, not even blood sorceries, can do that. Animalism is the only way to effectively mind control people into combat beyond a single good hit. If your players are trying to turn use Feral Infection to try and deal with people in a rational, non-violent way, that's just not what the power is designed for. That's what Majesty is for. And, to an extent, Nightmare via illusions and hallucinations. <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Marcus</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/849673-2ed-feral-infection?p=849703#post849703\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I suppose &quot;ride the wave&quot; is not an option here, right?</div> </div> </div> </div> Sure it is, but its expensive in terms of willpower. You can spend a point of willpower to ignore the directive of the Animalism user (any supernatural can spend wp to avoid the vampire's directive, but not the pseudo-frenzy), and then you need to spend willpower to do the actual riding of the wave. I don't see why its shouldn't be viable. Difficult, sure, but viable.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":2102,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2102-mcn","user":"MCN","date":". 03-19-2016, 11:47 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2102-mcn","name":"MCN","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2102_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3479"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-03-19T09:48:24-07:00","id":849775,"title":"","content":"Yes I meant that using Majesty 3 or 4 on the soldier leader, the Daeva could have convince him to let the prisioner go without the riot. <br /> I really don't know how to deal with the persuasion attempt over a crowd of fanatics...and Awe enhancs only the presence rolls not manipulation ones.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7079-marcus","name":"Marcus","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7079_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1119"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-03-19T10:13:21-07:00","id":849779,"title":"","content":"Presence + Persuasion or Expression (for a real speech or something) should work fine. I would think there would be lots of penalties for a crowd and for their predisposition, but Awe takes care of that.<br /> <br /> Why do you think you need to use manipulation? What do you think presence is for?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2698-the-storyteller","name":"The Storyteller","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"132"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-03-19T10:24:57-07:00","id":849782,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>The Storyteller</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/849673-2ed-feral-infection?p=849779#post849779\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Why do you think you need to use manipulation? What do you think presence is for?</div> </div> </div> </div>I think Presence is for the first impression, to attract the attention of someone with a look or to convince someone doing something for you just for your...presence (sweet eyes and stuff like this).<br /> Otherwise I see Manipulation something used to convince or persuade someone to do something with the strenght of your argumentation (or just of your words). But actually, yes, also presence it's a fair attribute for this situation. A VIP could convince his fans to do almost everything :P","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7079-marcus","name":"Marcus","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7079_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1119"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}